cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Knot Studio: quandle coloring and cocycle invariants for distinguishing prime knots with fewer than 10 crossings"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Li
    given-names: Xiang
    affiliation: "Guangdong Technion - Israel Institute of Technology (GTIIT), Shantou, China"
repository-code: "https://github.com/mikessslx/knot-studio"
url: "https://knot.cc.cd"
abstract: >-
  Interactive demo and research code that distinguishes prime knots with fewer than 10 crossings using quandle coloring counts and quandle 2-cocycle state-sum invariants. It encodes KnotInfo PD codes as a signed crossing-arc model, counts colorings by pruned depth-first search, Gaussian elimination over prime fields and Smith normal form over Z_n, selects a small distinguishing family of quandles by minimum set cover (integer programming), and refines that family with cocycle invariants.
keywords:
  - knot theory
  - quandle
  - cocycle invariant
  - set cover
  - computational topology
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-10-20"
references:
  - type: generic
    title: "KnotInfo: Table of Knot Invariants"
    authors:
      - family-names: Livingston
        given-names: Charles
      - family-names: Moore
        given-names: Allison H.
    url: "https://knotinfo.org"
    notes: "Source of the knot PD codes used in data/"
